<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-confuciusornis-sanctus-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Confuciusornis sanctus Turing wavelength at 143.4 µm (Yixian Fm, 125.0 Ma) — Code-to-model traceability: 84/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The docstring states Eqs. 1–5. critical_wavenumber, dispersion_sigma, predict_lambda_um, and the sweep each name the formula they implement. The Lean module proves the integer form of the trace, determinant, and instability inequality used by those functions. The split-step loop is not annotated line by line." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-confuciusornis-sanctus-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-confuciusornis-sanctus-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-confuciusornis-sanctus-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Confuciusornis sanctus Turing wavelength at 143.4 µm (Yixian Fm, 125.0 Ma) — Model fidelity to source: 88/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Equations 1–5, the periodic collar, and the integer mode-8 selection are unchanged and still self-tested. The Du sweep reproduces Eq. 5 (r = 0.9964) and the equal-diffusion ablation drives the pattern to roundoff, which is the Turing inequality in a spatial run. Six Lean theorems encode the trace, determinant, and cleared-denominator instability with zero sorry. Deduction: the kinetics remain a Schnakenberg carrier, not the feather papers' own ODEs." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "models/2026-delphi10000-confuciusornis-sanctus-turing-wavelength-s0.py L10–L17: docstring states the kinetics are a carrier, not a published feather table <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/fbd09a11bf97bd7e131df1afb92f62af0b4105ba/models/2026-delphi10000-confuciusornis-sanctus-turing-wavelength-s0.py#L10-L17>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-confuciusornis-sanctus-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-confuciusornis-sanctus-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-confuciusornis-sanctus-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Confuciusornis sanctus Turing wavelength at 143.4 µm (Yixian Fm, 125.0 Ma) — Morphometric validation: 90/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Measured versus analytic wavelength: Pearson r = 0.99643, RMSE = 4.975 µm, residual KS D = 0.160 (p = 0.980 against a normal with the residual mean and sd). At the canonical Du = 0.5 the measured peak is 145.14 µm against the analytic 143.4 µm, so the pair is not a copied scalar. Slab circularity 0.076 is scored against a disk reference of 1.0, coherency 0.565 against an isotropic prior of 0.2, foreground fraction 0.630 against 0.5. Ablation fold is 1.41e5 because the equal-diffusion std falls to 1.13e-6 while the Turing std stays 0.160." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-confuciusornis-sanctus-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-equal-diffusion-ablation-suppression>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-confuciusornis-sanctus-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-measured-collar-wavelength-at-du-0-5>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-confuciusornis-sanctus-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-specimen-contour-circularity>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-confuciusornis-sanctus-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-specimen-foreground-fraction>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-confuciusornis-sanctus-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-specimen-structure-tensor-coherency>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-confuciusornis-sanctus-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-wavelength-goodness-of-fit-pearson-r>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-confuciusornis-sanctus-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-wavelength-goodness-of-fit-rmse>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-confuciusornis-sanctus-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-wavelength-residual-ks-statistic>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-confuciusornis-sanctus-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-yixian-geological-age>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-confuciusornis-sanctus-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-confuciusornis-sanctus-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 9e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-confuciusornis-sanctus-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Confuciusornis sanctus Turing wavelength at 143.4 µm (Yixian Fm, 125.0 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 85.7/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 keeps the 143.4 µm, 125.0 Ma Schnakenberg collar and adds the four Pass 1 remediations. A Du sweep from 0.28 to 0.95 lengthens the measured dominant wavelength from 106.2 µm to 202.2 µm (Pearson r = 0.9964 against Eq. 5, RMSE = 4.97 µm, residual KS D = 0.160). Equal diffusion suppresses the activator standard deviation from 0.160 to 1.1e-6. The Senckenberg slab segments to foreground 0.630, circularity 0.076 (against a disk reference of 1), coherency 0.565. The 12-frame 640×480 GIF opens on the collar pattern and ends as a 90 percent register of the real photograph. Overall 85.7/100 (faithfulness 84.9, reproducibility 87.6); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit fbd09a11bf97bd7e131df1afb92f62af0b4105ba; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 88, Morphological realism / specimen match 78, Parameter expressivity 88, Morphometric validation 90, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 84, Reproducibility package 88. Output judged: docs/media/confuciusornis_sanctus_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-confuciusornis-sanctus-turing-wavelength-s0.py at fbd09a11bf97bd7e131df1afb92f62af0b4105ba, image/png, 479795 B, 1344×1008 px, artifact_sha256 25071a44c68f39447b5ba356630b29cd61f2c7c8d34ce46fcb81723d6ee4381f (sha256 25071a44c68f39447b5ba356630b29cd61f2c7c8d34ce46fcb81723d6ee4381f), spec_fingerprint eefa4e9a500552e28e1fe0176dd6aca52038d5438def2a8270217cfbd375bf34. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: eefa4e9a500552e28e1fe0176dd6aca52038d5438def2a8270217cfbd375bf34; artifact_sha256: 25071a44c68f39447b5ba356630b29cd61f2c7c8d34ce46fcb81723d6ee4381f; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/confuciusornis_sanctus_turing_wavelength_s0/confuciusornis_sanctus_specimen.jpg=9e83715a2090a049..., datasets/confuciusornis_sanctus_turing_wavelength_s0/confuciusornis_sanctus_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=95376a32ced97ca5..., datasets/confuciusornis_sanctus_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=969b2a6a15f61ba8...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-confuciusornis-sanctus-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing (1952) critical wavenumber from the dispersion relation | Within-feather pigment bars and spots are a reaction-diffusion pattern (Prum & Williamson 2002) | Barb-ridge spacing is an activator-inhibitor process (Harris et al. 2005) | Confuciusornis sanctus is a beaked pygostylian with ribbon rectrices and preserved feather pigment; reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg parameters chosen so analytic λ_c = 143.4 µm on an 8-mode periodic collar | Du sweep from 0.28 to 0.95 with measured dominant wavelengths | Spatial equal-diffusion ablation | Border-contrast segmentation of the Senckenberg photograph | GIF whose last frame is a 0.90/0.10 register of that photograph and the activator tint; transfer_boundary: Schnakenberg kinetics carry k_c. They are not a parameter table from Prum, Harris, or Hou. | 143.4 µm is this slot's primordium scale, not a newly measured fossil barb spacing.; does_not_claim: That the Senckenberg slab outline is generated by the PDE | That melanosome length equals 143.4 µm | A radiometric re-dating of the Yixian Formation." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "open need [independent_assessor/model-fidelity, pressure P=1.05]: A second assessor from another model has not scored this script.",
        "remediation needed: R1 resolved: Du sweep 0.28–0.95, measured λ monotone and tracked by Eq. 5",
        "remediation needed: R2 resolved: spatial equal-diffusion ablation, std 0.160 → 1.13e-6",
        "remediation needed: R3 resolved: slab segmentation (foreground 0.630, circularity 0.076, coherency 0.565) and GIF last-frame register",
        "remediation needed: R4 resolved: Pearson r = 0.9964, RMSE = 4.97 µm, KS D = 0.160; specimen metrics differ from their references" ;
    pk:hasScore 8.57e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-confuciusornis-sanctus-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Confuciusornis sanctus Turing wavelength at 143.4 µm (Yixian Fm, 125.0 Ma) — Parameter expressivity: 88/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Holding the ratio Dv/Du = 12 and the micrometre calibration fixed, Du from 0.28 to 0.95 moves the measured dominant wavelength monotonically 106.2 → 124.7 → 142.8 → 145.1 → 163.0 → 186.8 → 202.2 µm, in the direction Eq. 5 predicts (longer diffusion length, longer wave). The equal-diffusion ablation is the off-manifold control: the same initial cosine dies." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-confuciusornis-sanctus-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-confuciusornis-sanctus-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-confuciusornis-sanctus-turing-wavelength-s0-repro-package> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Confuciusornis sanctus Turing wavelength at 143.4 µm (Yixian Fm, 125.0 Ma) — Reproducibility package: 88/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Seed 3152, fixed sweep grid, --self-test (r > 0.98, monotone Du sweep, ablation fold > 5, elongated slab), and pinned input hashes. The render writes a 640×480 12-frame GIF and the comparison PNG. Deduction: no per-script lockfile, and `lean` is not installed in this environment so the proofs were not kernel-checked here." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-repro-package> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
