    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-confuciusornis-sanctus-turing-wavelength-s0.py, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_3152_confuciusornis_sanctus_turing_wavelength_s0.lean; output: docs/media/confuciusornis_sanctus_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Confuciusornis sanctus; environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing (1952) critical wavenumber from the dispersion relation | Within-feather pigment bars and spots are a reaction-diffusion pattern (Prum & Williamson 2002) | Barb-ridge spacing is an activator-inhibitor process (Harris et al. 2005) | Confuciusornis sanctus is a beaked pygostylian with ribbon rectrices and preserved feather pigment; reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg parameters chosen so analytic λ_c = 143.4 µm on an 8-mode periodic collar | Du sweep from 0.28 to 0.95 with measured dominant wavelengths | Spatial equal-diffusion ablation | Border-contrast segmentation of the Senckenberg photograph | GIF whose last frame is a 0.90/0.10 register of that photograph and the activator tint; transfer_boundary: Schnakenberg kinetics carry k_c. They are not a parameter table from Prum, Harris, or Hou. | 143.4 µm is this slot's primordium scale, not a newly measured fossil barb spacing.; does_not_claim: That the Senckenberg slab outline is generated by the PDE | That melanosome length equals 143.4 µm | A radiometric re-dating of the Yixian Formation]; phenomenon_size: 109 µm (0.0001086 m, log10=-3.964 m, tier=5_primordium_100um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 109 µm to 24.4 cm): 109 µm:confuciusornis-sanctus-bioelectric-polarity, 340 µm:confuciusornis-sanctus-vertex-packing, 5.4 mm:confuciusornis-sanctus-turing-wavelength, 1.1 cm:confuciusornis-sanctus-clock-wavefront, 2.4 cm:confuciusornis-sanctus-morphogen-condensation, 3.0 cm:confuciusornis-sanctus-elastic-buckling, 3.4 cm:confuciusornis-sanctus-flux-canalization, 4.